            0.341,
            0.726,
            0.78,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "contributions to several areas of science. In the nineteenth century, Faraday delivered a series of lectures called Chemical History of a Candle. Faraday believed that the candle was the perfect object to introduce scientific study. Through it, he discussed differences between various physical and chemical processes like melting, vapourisation, and combustion."
            }
          ],
